    {
      "advice": [
        {
          "references": [
            "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-directory#cleaned-up-automatically",
            "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings"
          ],
          "snippets": [
            "{ \"cleanupPeriodDays\": 14 }"
          ],
          "text": "cleanupPeriodDays in your user settings: 14 days, from <demo>/home/.claude/settings.json. Claude Code deletes transcripts, file history, plans, debug logs and other session data older than this. The default is 30 and the minimum 1; 0 fails validation. Managed settings, and project or command-line settings, override the user setting, and kipple doesn't read them. It never deletes auto memory files (versions before v2.1.228 could delete old files below a memory directory), keeps Claude Desktop and Cowork transcripts unless desktopSessionCleanupPeriodDays is set, and doesn't sweep in --bare sessions.",
          "title": "Claude Code's own transcript retention"
        }
      ],
